From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hans2294 <22217531+hans2294@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:09:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu_kms: A tear-free desktop with Haiku's own app_server

app_server gets a shadow in RAM as its frame buffer, and a thread flips: the
driver tells which pages were written to, from the page tables' dirty bits, and
they go into the hidden half of a double buffer. It waits for the writes to pause
first, for up to half a refresh, as app_server doesn't say when it is done. GL and
Vulkan don't draw straight into the frame buffer then. A patched app_server that
asks for a double height mode does its own flipping, as before.

Measured with a capture dongle, an 800x600 window going black and white: 451 of
451 frames torn without it, 41 with it; 1 at 60 fills/s, 0 at 30 fills/s or less.

tearingtest can pace its fills.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
