index 641f66bfbb..58a0cadc84 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/accelerants/amdgpu_kms/accelerant.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/accelerants/amdgpu_kms/accelerant.cpp
@@ -18,7 +18,16 @@
 	A mode twice as high as the display (virtual_height) gets a buffer for
 	two screens, with a KMS framebuffer for each half; B_MOVE_DISPLAY picks
 	the half to show with a page flip at the next vblank, and returns once
-	it is shown. app_server flips like that for a tear-free desktop.
+	it is shown. A patched app_server flips like that for a tear-free desktop.
+
+	Haiku's own app_server asks for no such thing, and draws straight into the
+	frame buffer. It then gets a shadow in RAM as its frame buffer, and a thread
+	does the flipping: the driver tells which of the shadow's pages were written
+	to, they go into the hidden half, and it flips. That leaves the picture alone
+	while the display scans it out. Since app_server doesn't say when it is done
+	drawing, the thread waits for the writes to stop, and a program that draws
+	without pause can still show something half drawn. TEAR_FREE=0 in the
+	environment turns the shadow off.
 */
 
 
